  "mathematical_review": {
    "fixed_cones_and_six_player_contribution": "The21 frozen complete policies have one commonQ for each entire exact IC cone; lambda(p)=n sum p_a lambda_a constructs fixed-query(T) instances. This is checks/context for the generic minimax/Farkas equivalence, not a proof of that whole theorem. On the single b352 n6/k8 cone, ALL{commonQ certificate, same-instance static OPT6<=11v6} yields W>=6v6>=6OPT6/11, hence half. Integer unit customers and positive rational denominator scaling are explicit; arbitrary other sigma/k and the whole exact-six target remain open.",
    "two_path_tail_rows": "ALL{T2 tax, fullT3 background residual, original1499/750 T4 residual} proves exactly1416 tail rows on actualABCDE and same-sigma forcedEQRST. Each path has46/166/496 rows; the96-cell r3 keeps d=0 credit and the same32-cell r4 is charged five times. ForcedE is not a BR; all successors are true. Model reasoning supplies90 safe rows plusrootE. The exact LP value and its16-atom/14-multiplier certificate remain separate. At that relaxation point both N5 inequalities hold, both half-payment conditions fail, and the richer current five-playerhalf certificate is compatible.",
    "thirteen_player_endpoint": "The complete fixed13-player36-customer witness in M7v3, not an abstract delta-failure implication, gives the exact M05v2 ENT1 counterexample: g=(5/3,3/2,3,5/2,5/2,25/11),R0=359/66,M1=3 and gap37/66. B=W-R0 makes SAIC the same assertion, so the whole target is obtained by one accepted implication. Reverse relay/matrix/query information is not obtained from the static endpoint. Credit normalization is retained: adjusted_total_delta12704/5577 and fully overlap-adjusted excess-179225/11154. The formal weak-family comparison is closed as a distinct scaled all-m target, while generic exists-good-optimal-query/payment remains open.",
    "cross9311": "Three independent contributions retain their distinct roles: strongPAIR supplies60RZ+60ZZ indexed row families with one positive overlap; the basic split supplies56 true diagonal/offdiagonal rows using30/6 index counts and exact four-state substitution; the whole-catalog safe bound excludes every complete SPE completion preserving the fixed actual/hist/R identity, whateverZ or unknown continuation is used. Common theta is shared within each R layer, so intersections are sums of layerwise minima, not minima of total marginals. The38-atom catalogue and uniform six-index averaging establish membership realization and OPT6=1 only; the four negative fixedR safe sums still prevent SPE realization. Numerical9311 feasibility is its own mature evidence.",
    "early_follower": "The explicit six-slack decomposition with weights(35,11,3,10,12,3) and the same fourth source yields210u4+132u6+18K>=sum psi_i. Joint four-state D/E minimization preserves the originalB_i/C_i joint marginal and two separate actual-last-price wallets. The sameSHA3889-point has exact negative left-right; thus the complete registered local noncompletion statement follows.2560 author and1024/256 parent checks are two qualifications of one formula and point. The1269 feasible relaxation and third-position153-row separation are not premises or extra counterexamples.",
    "new60_terminal_envelope": "True AB terminal nodes use p=a+b+t+rAB. The two AE legal query menus share one tuple matching in each commonT group. Their nonnegative O rows have a jointly sorted per-customer upper envelope with a strictly negative total at the fixedSHA11a26c60-point, so no marginal-preserving full SPE completion exists. Both individual O envelopes are already negative; this point does not demonstrate joint-only strictness. The general convex-separation converse is optional interpretation, not an additional needed ALL premise.557 feasibility/O/70zeros and the two-tail strongPAIR negative rows retain separate evidence and are not supplied by the terminal theorem.",
    "no_new_cross_archive_transfer": "These six packets compare customer-attraction results and its six-provider restriction. No unrelated archive model is identified merely by a shared name or formula. Prior cross-archive reviews and their authorship remain intact."
  },
